488 0 obj
<<
/Title (Performance optimization in low-code applications means designing forms, workflows and scripts so that they use data and processing only as far as needed. Although a low-code platform handles much of the underlying work, the way in which a workflow is written still influences how efficiently it runs.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 434 0 R
/Next 489 0 R
>>
endobj
489 0 obj
<<
/Title (Retrieving more records than required, or repeatedly processing records that are not relevant to the task, causes unnecessary data retrieval and processing. In a small application this may not be noticeable, but as the number of book issue requests and users grows it can reduce application efficiency. Efficient workflows in Zoho Creator therefore retrieve only the data they need and avoid unnecessary processing, which supports scalable and maintainable applications.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 434 0 R
/Prev 488 0 R
>>
endobj
